# The integration-layer CLI plugin (@commercetools/cli-topic-integration-layer) is
# published to the PUBLIC npm registry. The @commercetools scope resolves there by
# default, so no scope mapping and no committed token are needed:
#
#   - install: `pnpm install` / `commercetools plugins install` resolve from
#     registry.npmjs.org with no auth (the package and all its deps are public).
#   - publish: CI uses npm Trusted Publishing (OIDC) — actions/setup-node with
#     `registry-url` + `id-token: write` injects a short-lived token at publish
#     time. There is no NPM_TOKEN to store or rotate. See publish-release.yml.
